WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
So, as you start to master Claude code,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.470
I actually wanted to give you a

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.310
framework and a mental model of how to

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.590
approach this. So that as you use Claude

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.710
code more and more, it actually becomes

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.470
stronger, more efficient, more

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.270
effective, and just so much better for

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.030
you on day 100 than what it was on day

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.110
one. And there's actually one model that

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.110
will unlock this for you. Because if you

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.310
remember, every agent platform, whether

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.070
it's Claude code, Open Claw, Hermes, or

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.350
even Codex or Anti-Gravity, it's always

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.990
just composed of three basic elements.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.790
You have the model, which functions as

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.150
the engine or the brain of your AI

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.870
agent, and you also have as a second

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.150
layer, the harness, which is Claude code

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.910
itself. And Claude code in its essence

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.030
is just a set of system prompts, it's a

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.590
set of coding files that just wraps the

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.830
model so that it can actually use tools,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.750
use your computer, edit your files for

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.670
you on your behalf. But the key thing to

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.630
remember is that the model, as well as

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.510
the harness, all of us are using the

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.110
same thing, right? So if you're using

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.510
Claude code, we're using the same

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.070
harness, and we're also using the same

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.070
models. But the key differentiator that

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.549
we can affect as users is our context,

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:06.550
which is our workspace, essentially. And

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.150
so therein lies your edge. Because if

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.830
everyone has the same model and everyone

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.350
is using the same harness, if you

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.870
actually engineer your context properly

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.230
and you have proper control of your

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.230
context for your business as well as

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.510
your personal work, and you're very

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.630
effective with letting your agent use

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.190
that context to give you a competitive

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.110
advantage, then you are already at the

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.830
top 1% of Claude code users. And just to

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.630
give you a quick reminder put it in

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.270
perspective of how advanced you are. If

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.350
this is the global population of around

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.270
8 billion people, then you can see that

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.190
a vast majority of the global population

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.350
still has never used AI, and this is as

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.990
of February 2026. These in green are

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.950
free chatbot users, so you may know that

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.310
ChatGPT has something like 900 million

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.310
weekly active users. So this is that

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.990
cohort. So your relatives, maybe your

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.590
parents, have used ChatGPT before, then

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:57.870
they are part of this green section.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.550
Now, those who actually have visibility

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.270
on the most advanced models are the ones

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.390
in yellow, which are the ones who are

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.190
paying at least $20 per month for AI,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.070
and they comprise a really small part of

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.750
the population. Now, where you are is in

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.590
this red square. You are using already a

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.470
coding scaffold, which is basically an

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.590
authentic harness like Cloud Code. So,

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.790
if you're part of this community and

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.350
you're watching this, then remember that

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.110
you are at the very forefront of this

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.070
technology. And so, from within that red

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.270
circle, the way that you get ahead is

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.230
actually by managing your context and by

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.949
applying a framework that will put you

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:32.550
ahead. And just to make it really

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.510
simple, if you think about your AI

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.990
agents as your digital employees, where

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.190
when you're hiring them, they're coming

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.990
with their own engine, basically their

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.190
brain, which is the model, and they're

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.870
also coming with their own harness,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.230
similar to how a car that only has an

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.830
engine, but it also comes with the body

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.190
of the car. Now, when you think about

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.550
this analogy, the context is basically

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.350
your workspace. And as I've mentioned

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.790
previously, a workspace is just a folder

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.510
in your machine, in your computer. For

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.310
me specifically, I just assign this

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.470
folder called Robo in my workspace,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.310
where it has all the context for my

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.110
business. It has all of the code and

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.910
automations included in here, and you

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.430
can even see some images and videos that

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.790
are contained from just within this file

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.670
folder. And the power of engineering

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.150
this context in a way that is effective

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.990
is that it actually starts to become

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.030
your operating system. And if you think

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.790
about an operating system, what is that

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.870
essentially? Well, to me, that is

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.110
basically the base layer that everything

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.750
runs on, right? So, whenever I open my

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.590
device now, the very first thing that I

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.310
open is Cloud Code. It's the first thing

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:32.310
that I use, is the all-in-one software

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.430
and teammate that I now talk to on a

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.990
daily and hourly basis in order to get

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.870
work done. And so, it's now become the

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.710
base layer by which all of our business

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.790
and my personal work runs in. So, the

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.470
question now becomes, how do you now get

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.229
to this point where you have Cloud Code

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:48.949
as your operating system, which is

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:51.190
giving you 10x productivity and unfair

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.230
advantages over your competition in a

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.990
way that doesn't confuse you. Well, in

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.590
this masterclass, what I'll be going

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.670
through and also breaking down for you

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.830
is this arms framework. I'm calling it

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.390
arms because, number one, it's so much

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.110
easier to remember with a proper

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.910
acronym. And number two, it is sort of

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.150
like giving your AI agents their own

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.350
arms to reach out to your workspace, to

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.750
your contacts in order to do the work

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.390
that you need them to do. And the key

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.310
with this framework is that if you have

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.870
Cloud Code set up so that it can access

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.190
and connect to your applications and

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.670
where it has routines or scheduled tasks

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.470
that run in the background even without

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.670
you. Plus, it has the memory and all of

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.670
the context of your business and your

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.750
personal work. And finally, all of the

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.270
skills so that it can perform all of the

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.150
tasks that you assign to it in a manner

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.070
that is aligned with the output that you

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.590
are expecting. Then you'll be able to

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.630
reach a point when your Cloud Code is a

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.870
proper teammate that actually automates

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.909
work for you and giving you productivity

00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:47.909
gains that you never imagined would be

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:50.150
possible before. And so, back to our

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.110
analogy. Remember that your agent, Cloud

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.790
Code, which comes with its model and its

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:55.830
harness, the digital employee that you

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.030
hired, all you're setting up for them is

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.150
their workspace. So, this analogy will

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.070
explore a bit more to make it simpler

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.550
for you to understand how these

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.550
different pillars work together. But you

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.990
can imagine that if you're setting up a

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.830
workspace for a new employee, you

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.390
basically would need to give them access

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.630
to applications on their device. You

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:14.670
also need to give your agent a set of

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.870
routines or schedules so that it can

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.790
follow and understand the tasks that

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.870
recur in its calendar, which it should

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.670
also have in its workspace. Then you

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.190
have the memory component, which is, in

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.550
its essence, just a filing cabinet of

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:27.870
all the conversations and all the

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.470
projects that you have done together so

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.390
that it can retrieve them whenever they

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.710
are relevant. And finally, the skills

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.510
would be sort of their notebook with

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.470
different recipe cards or instruction

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.790
cards that let them recall how to do a

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.950
specific task. And so, if you think

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.630
about this framework in this analogy, it

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.750
becomes so much easier to remember it.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:48.710
Just to make sure that your agent is as

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.910
effective as it can be. And so, in this

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.750
masterclass, we'll be learning this

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.790
bottoms-up, which is my recommended

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.070
method where we start first with giving

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.150
you knowledge of the skills and how to

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.950
